<Layout title="Word Problems Worksheets – Proportions, Area, Multiplication & Division | Math Worksheet Studio"
description="Generate original, reproducible math word-problem worksheets for unit rates, rectangular area, multiplication and equal-sharing division. Download matching student, answer and worked-step PDFs." canonicalPath="/word-problems-worksheets/">
<div class="container">
<section class="hero hero-compact">
<div class="crumb"><a href="/worksheets/">All math worksheets</a> / Applied arithmetic</div>
<span class="eyebrow">Original stories · Exact arithmetic · Separate answers</span>
<h1>Word Problems Worksheets</h1>
<p>Practice reading a real-world situation, deciding which operation fits, and writing the answer with units. Generate new word problems or focus on one of four supported skills.</p>
</section>
<WordProblems/>
<section class="info-grid">
<div class="panel info-panel">
<span class="eyebrow">What's inside</span>
<h2>Four different word-problem skills</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Proportions:</strong> Find a unit rate and scale it to another number of batches. Example: 12 cups for 3 batches requires 20 cups for 5 batches.</li>
<li><strong>Area:</strong> Multiply a rectangular garden's length and width. Example: a 7 ft × 4 ft bed covers 28 square feet.</li>
<li><strong>Multiplication:</strong> Combine equal groups. Example: 6 boxes of 8 markers contain 48 markers.</li>
<li><strong>Division:</strong> Divide a collection into equal shares. Example: 42 pencils shared by 7 students gives 6 pencils each.</li>
</ul>
<p>The mixed setting rotates all four types. Every PDF uses the same exact seeded problem set, and answers and steps are in separate editions.</p>
</div>
<div class="panel info-panel">
<span class="eyebrow">Teaching notes</span>
<h2>From reading to a mathematical model</h2>
<ol>
<li>Underline the quantities, units and what the question is asking.</li>
<li>Identify a constant rate, rectangular dimensions or an equal-groups situation.</li>
<li>Calculate with the correct operation; for proportions, first find the unit rate.</li>
<li>Check whether the answer's units match the question before reading the teacher key.</li>
</ol>
<p>Scope: whole-number rates, one-step rectangle area, equal groups and exact equal sharing. This tool does <strong>not</strong> claim compound interest, percentage discounts, unequal-remainder stories, multistep algebra, or certified grade alignment.</p>
</div>
</section>
